      "name": "Pachycephala",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The typical whistlers — a large genus of stocky, big-headed passerines known for their extraordinarily loud, clear, melodic whistles that carry long distances through the forest. They are found from Southeast Asia through Australasia to the Pacific islands. Despite their small size, they have disproportionately large, rounded heads, which gives them their scientific name meaning 'thick head'.",
